## 6. why G-161-5 is NOT closed
- GitHub docs (Managing environments for deployment): 'Running a workflow that references an environment that does not exist will create an environment with the referenced name … the newly created environment will not have any protection rules or secrets configured.' The docs do not say what a SKIPPED job referencing an environment does.
- The design never names r161-staging in an environment key; the live job's name is ${{ needs.gate.outputs.environment }}, set only after the gate verified the environment ALREADY exists with reviewers and a main-only branch policy. Proven statically and by unit tests — NOT by a GitHub run: dispatching the workflow is outside this batch's authorization (it could create a repository resource).
- Anyone with write access can dispatch a modified copy of the workflow from another branch; a platform property, not controllable from this file.

